WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.302
We've got brand new video into CNN.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.237
It shows a huge caravan of vehicles

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.805
trying to leave the desert.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.141
You see how large that lineup

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:08.942
actually is.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:09.642
That's in Nevada

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.111
at the Burning Man Festival.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.212
The good news today.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.146
The sun is shining,

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:13.980
which means the road

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.049
to get out of the festival is drying.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.150
Officials have said that

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:17.751
next hour

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.386
they expect more people to begin

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.220
to head out.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.121
Tens of thousands,

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.055
though, have been stranded

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:22.555
in the mud

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.356
for days

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.158
after two to three months of rain

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.594
swamped the area in just 24 hours.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.662
I talked to one attendee last hour

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.630
and here's what she said

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.400
about the situation on the ground that

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.503
there's a really, really long line

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.270
trying to get out.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.571
Some people are leaving,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.873
I think mostly the four wheel

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.808
drives, the super type vehicles,

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.309
not the passenger cars yet.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.611
There are a few of those stuck.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:45.512
Or as you drive,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.946
you're going to accumulate mud

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.782
on those tires and those seats.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.949
It makes everything harder

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.151
and you don't want to get stuck in this

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.185
and then prevent other people

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.186
from leaving.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.320
So it's everybody's

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.422
being really cool about it.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.057
We're just biding our time.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.893
CNN national correspondent

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.028
Nic White is covering this story for us.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.630
So what is the latest

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.631
that officials are saying about

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.565
when these roads

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.132
could reopen

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.866
in a safe way

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.069
to start getting people out?

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.804
Well, the latest we heard,

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:13.540
Omar, is in about an hour from now.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.775
They say that for the moment,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:16.943
the roads are still too

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.012
wet and muddy for most vehicles,

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:19.946
but not all.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.414
We have seen some four wheel

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.415
drive vehicles

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.751
getting out late last night and also

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.719
this morning, you know.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.189
70 plus thousand people stuck in there.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:29.589
And CNN

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:30.857
is spoken to some of those

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.592
who've managed to get out so far.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.560
And they describe,

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.761
you know, as seen on Saturday,

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.962
everyone waiting for

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.664
that man to be burned,

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.499
the kind of climax of this festival.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.334
The rain started and initially,

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:41.568
you know,

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.902
people were dancing in the mud,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.770
having a good time.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.904
And then gradually

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.172
there was a realization.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.340
Hang on a second.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.041
We're not going to be able

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.342
to get out of this.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.076
You mentioned that

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.878
the sun is right now key.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.380
What happens is that is Clay.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.683
It's a dried up ancient lake.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.552
The rain comes makes it totally slick.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.855
The water just sticks on top.

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:03.823
Which makes it hugely problematic

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.290
to get out.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:04.924
But also,

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.658
if the rain

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.726
the water is still on top,

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.194
that means the sun can dry it.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.430
And that's what we're seeing right now.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:11.431
You know,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.398
there is an ethos of kind

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:14.400
of self-reliance around this festival.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.602
And a lot of people did

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.536
bring in everything

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:19.639
they needed to survive for a few days.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.640
They were planning to be there

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.541
and a little bit extra

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.476
But we have heard that some people were

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.544
not so well prepared

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.613
and it got pretty terrible for people.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.181
There camps were washed away.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.316
It's the desert. It got cold at night.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:31.317
And then, of course,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.552
Omar, there were some people

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:33.520
who walked out,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.322
including a little clique of celebrities,

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:37.757
including Chris Rock.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.226
I'll let DJ Diplo take up that story.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:41.161
Take a listen.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.798
That is New York Knicks.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.366
Check it out.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.400
We just he just got up with us

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.735
and started walking

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.136
and we walked about 3 hours

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.839
in the mud and he was happy with me.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:54.040
I think Cindy Crawford

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.742
walked through this Kaia Gerber,

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.577
Austin Butler,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.512
Randy Gerber,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.948
a writer, a couple producers from TV,

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:02.715
a couple people who just wanted

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:03.750
to get home to their children.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.019
And they didn't take no for an answer.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.224
So those walkers managed

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.560
to get to an actual road out of the mud

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.561
after a few hours.

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.863
And a guy in a passing pickup truck

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.865
apparently recognized DJ Diplo

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.966
and gave them a ride.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:23.169
And eventually they all made it to Reno.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:24.204
But during the day

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.572
today, Omar, we're going to try

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.673
and hopefully

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:29.909
see the mass exodus, the 70,000

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:30.877
plus people coming out.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.213
But some people are going to stick it out

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.813
a little bit longer

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.714
because they plan

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.916
to burn the man tonight.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.384
So there are people

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.520
who want to stay there until the end.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.421
And, you know,

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.456
they'll just be praying for no more rain

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.124
and there is no more rain

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.426
in the forecast.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:49.662
So fingers crossed Omar starts to walk

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:50.496
from Diplo.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.397
But hopefully for the folks

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.665
that are left behind,

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.100
they get some relief very soon.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.435
Nick Watt, thank you very much.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.971
Let's get you a picture now

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.339
of the situation on the ground

00:03:59.339 --> 00:03:59.906
at Burning Man

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.107
with a festival go

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:01.441
where Cutter

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.342
Palacios is

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.977
on the ground there right now.

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.045
Cutter, thanks so much for being with us.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.281
So the organizers say the departures

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.415
officially are set to begin

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.650
in about an hour.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.385
I'm wondering what your plan is.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:15.855
Are you planning to leave or stick around

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.157
We're going to see the burn.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.125
I think it's great

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.026
because they're doing

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.127
all three burns tonight.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.696
So the man's at nine.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:27.734
The Chapel of Babble is

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.402
is at midnight

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.437
and in the temples at 1 a.m..

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.438
So this is awesome.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.873
We are hoping to leave by Tuesday

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:34.574
or Wednesday.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.475
And the fact that we're doing it

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.577
all in one night of celebration

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.178
and then we're going to join

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.813
the mass exodus of people

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.982
in line

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.551
for hours and hours tomorrow.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.920
And then we get home.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.788
Middle of the night,

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:51.424
but we stay on Wednesday nights.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.925
So cover for folks

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:55.762
that are not initiated in the rituals

00:04:55.762 --> 00:04:58.698
and the ethos, the spirit of Burning Man.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.333
What is it that drives

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:02.402
so many people out there to the desert?

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.603
Because it kind of surprises me

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.538
that you're saying this is awesome.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.473
While it looks from the outside

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.775
like a mess,

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.745
it's messy.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:13.713
Yeah.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.615
I think that's sort of the thrill of it.

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:16.215
I mean,

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.950
certainly people come out here

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:18.384
and they're winning

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.419
the festival experience,

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.753
but the majority of us

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:21.954
are winning some great community

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.823
or wanting to create a city

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:24.991
from essentially nothing.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.492
We bring in our self-reliance

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:26.926
or radical

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:28.328
self-reliance and

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:31.130
a big spirit is gifting.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.132
Last night we had a neighboring tent

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:34.200
because we're not part of the camp,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.635
but we had a neighboring camp

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:36.569
giving out pizza

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:38.104
and they had vegan pizza.

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:40.173
So we just all sat around a fire

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.908
eating pizza.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:42.909
I have a friend down

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:43.710
at the French Quarter

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.978
who is like serving up lobster, you know,

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.247
which is a real treat.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.749
And for those who are in need,

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:51.084
we all help each other out.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.151
And that's just

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:52.785
that's not something

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.721
that you get to see every day

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:55.621
and you get to experience

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.589
for an entire week,

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.157
especially through these hardships.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.325
Really, took care of one another.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:01.327
And I think that's that's incredible.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.161
That is incredible.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.430
Especially lobster and vegan pizza.

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:05.264
It sounds like you have

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.666
basic necessities covered

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.371
in food, shelter, water.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:11.671
You know,

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:12.105
that's really

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:14.273
what you need to be out here.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.609
I did not plan for rain.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.277
I didn't bring a raincoat

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.046
but we were improvising.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:22.115
We use trash bags.

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:23.416
There is definitely some foot

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.017
where those being improvised.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.486
Some people are going barefoot.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.587
And there was like

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:29.389
the plastic bag over the sock.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:30.823
No, no, no. It's a plastic bag.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:31.557
And then the sock.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.992
And then eventually the radio came out

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:33.826
and told us

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:36.929
it was a shoe and the sock over the shoe.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:38.231
I don't know about all that.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:40.133
I just went with a tried and true sock

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.401
and the shoe over sock,

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.902
and that seemed to work for me.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:43.870
So I'm

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.138
glad I'm glad you were able to

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:47.240
find a system to get through the mud.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.541
There were reports, though, Cutter,

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.542
I want to ask you about this.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.544
There were reports that misinformation

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:54.347
was spreading around festival goers,

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.582
rumors, false rumors.

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.684
I should point out about Ebola spreading.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.520
A SWAT team at one point was called in

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.988
because a shooting was reported.

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:03.423
Did you come across any of that

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:07.860
I don't know about Ebola.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.328
I will say

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.730
and I don't know about the SWAT team,

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:11.664
but we did

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.533
get police vehicles

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.535
coming through the walk in were

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.804
we're out at two 30 and walk in,

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.373
which is where there's no cars allowed.

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:23.443
Police did did respond very quickly

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.913
to whatever that report was.

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.381
I think it's important to note,

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:29.649
like in terms of communication,

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.050
there's not a lot of communication

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:31.951
out here.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:34.020
You have a radio

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.556
and they are doing the best they can

00:07:36.556 --> 00:07:38.458
to communicate accurate information

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:39.692
from from officials

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:40.927
and from outside sources.

00:07:40.927 --> 00:07:42.128
But just listening

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:43.863
to the CNN stuff going on you

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:44.464
that's more news

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:45.131
I've heard

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:47.900
since I've been out here for a week.

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:50.570
Congrats to the astronauts landing.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.139
But yeah, it's word of mouth

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:55.541
and and that's really cool, too.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:58.044
And you do the best you can.

00:07:58.044 --> 00:07:59.145
And one of the principles out here

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.213
is immediacy.

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.047
You know, it

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:01.981
generally means that

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:02.815
you see something cool

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:03.549
and you're call to

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:04.984
go and participate in it

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:07.286
and help out and explore

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:08.821
and live life out here.

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:11.357
And it also means that news

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.792
and word of mouth,

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:15.995
it's it's moment to moment as well.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:16.863
That makes sense.

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:18.197
We're really glad that you're doing well.

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.665
I hope you enjoy that lobster

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.867
and the vegan pizza.

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:22.034
And I hope

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.302
you get to enjoy the burnings tonight

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:26.005
and a smooth ride back home to you.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:26.739
Cutter Palacios,

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:27.707
thanks so much for being with us.

